@format 1
@id keyframes.next
@title Move to next keyframe
@area 3. Keyframes and waveform
@entry input
@summary Resolve the earliest stored keyframe after the cursor only after contiguous scan coverage proves that the candidate is valid.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related keyframes.scan, keyframes.previous, keyframes.nearest

@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow
@alias key = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LKeyframeOrchestrator

[input] Next-keyframe command <input>
- Dispatch the next-keyframe shortcut when timeline commands and a spool are active @ flow.PFlowShortcutDispatch(...)
> find

[find] Resolve a covered following point <decision>
- Find the least stored timestamp in the forward search range @ key.LKeyframeMoveResolve(...)
- Require every scan span between the cursor and candidate, or the cursor and search boundary when no candidate exists, to be current @ key.LKeyframeMoveResolve(...)
? "Coverage is current and a candidate exists" > move
? "Coverage is current and no candidate exists" > unavailable
? "Required coverage is incomplete" > scan

[move] Move to stored candidate <process>
- Accept the non-null stored candidate and propagate it as the new cursor @ flow.PFlowKeyframeMove(...)
- Update both timeline views, request a scan around the new position, and seek the preview @ flow.PFlowCursorPropagate(...)
> result

[result] Next keyframe selected <output>
= The cursor moves only to a candidate proven by contiguous scanned coverage.

[unavailable] No next keyframe <output>
= The covered forward search range contains no next keyframe, so the cursor remains unchanged.

[scan] Scan around the unchanged cursor <process>
- Keep the next-keyframe command pending and start a focused scan immediately @ flow.PFlowKeyframeMove(...)
> wait

[wait] Re-evaluate current scan notices <process>
- Retry the pending command whenever a source-current scan notice updates keyframes and covered ranges @ flow.PFlowNoticeHandle(...)
> find
